<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theocles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 734 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theocles was the leader of the Greek colonists from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcis">Chalcis</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euboea">Euboea</a> who founded Naxos around 734 BCE, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thucydides">Thucydides</a> the first Greek colony in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. Thucydides also records that a few years later he led settlers from Naxos to found Leontini. He is known only from these ancient accounts of the colonisation of Sicily.</p></div>
